# The base is a value that nobody knows, so Worker goes under an object that native code holds, and Worker.prototype under whatever that object has as its prototype.
# A lookup on an instance that misses on Worker.prototype goes on into the unknown: `on` may be anything, and the instance is handed to it.
# The method that the program stores on Worker.prototype is still found by name.
# With a base of the program: flow/calls/to-class-is-followed-through-its-model.ir
# RUN: flow-links calls unknown
# RUN(SINKS): flow-solve sinks
# CHECK: f0 v5 -> {{*}} f6 Call
# CHECK: f0 v20 -> {{*}} f3 Call
# CHECK: unknown-callee {{*}} v22 Call
# SINKS: nativeCode {{*}}L0#

